{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Best cards for a purchase"},"description":"Ranks every card earnrate knows that takes new applicants, not only the user's, for one purchase or category, each set up at its best (the right category pick, activated, cap unused), with its annual fee and what earning the rate takes. Use it for questions like \"what's the best card for groceries?\" or \"which card should I get for Amazon?\". It needs no wallet. For which of the user's own cards to use, call best_card_for_purchase instead. Mention the annual fee and any conditions alongside each card. Cards that need a membership the user hasn't given (Verizon Visa) are in `membersOnly`, not the ranking: name them after it, as the text does. For a store, cards with a statement credit there come first in `credits` (\"$75 back each quarter, then 1x Amex Membership Rewards\"): present them first, in dollars and never as a percentage, saying when the cardholder must enroll, then the ranking by rate.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"amount":{"description":"Purchase amount in US dollars, if known.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"business":{"description":"Business cards instead of personal ones.","type":"boolean"},"category":{"description":"A spending category: dining (Restaurants), dining.fast_food (Fast food), grocery.supermarket (Supermarkets), grocery.online (Online grocery and delivery), superstore (Superstores), warehouse_club (Warehouse clubs), convenience_store (Convenience stores), gas (Gas stations), gas.grocery_store (Gas at grocery stores), gas.superstore (Gas at superstores and warehouse clubs), ev_charging (EV charging), transit (Transit), transit.rideshare (Rideshare and taxis), travel (Travel), travel.flights (Flights), travel.hotels (Hotels), travel.car_rental (Car rentals), travel.cruise (Cruises), streaming (Streaming services), tv_internet (TV and internet service), phone (Cell phone service), utilities (Home utilities), housing (Rent and mortgage), drugstore (Drugstores and pharmacies), movie_theaters (Movie theaters), entertainment (Live entertainment and events), fitness (Gyms and fitness), department_store (Department stores), clothing (Clothing stores), electronics (Electronics stores), sporting_goods (Sporting goods stores), home_improvement (Home improvement), furniture (Furniture stores), online_retail (Online retail), office_supply (Office supply stores), shipping (Shipping and couriers), online_advertising (Social media and search advertising), other (Everything else).","enum":["dining","dining.fast_food","grocery.supermarket","grocery.online","superstore","warehouse_club","convenience_store","gas","gas.grocery_store","gas.superstore","ev_charging","transit","transit.rideshare","travel","travel.flights","travel.hotels","travel.car_rental","travel.cruise","streaming","tv_internet","phone","utilities","housing","drugstore","movie_theaters","entertainment","fitness","department_store","clothing","electronics","sporting_goods","home_improvement","furniture","online_retail","office_supply","shipping","online_advertising","other"],"type":"string"},"channel":{"description":"How the purchase is made. Omit if unknown; the answer says what it assumed.","enum":["online","in_store"],"type":"string"},"country":{"description":"Where the purchase is made, as a two-letter country code (FR, GB, JP). Pass it when the user is paying abroad or in another currency: abroad, cards are ranked after their foreign transaction fees. Default US.","pattern":"^[A-Za-z]{2}$","type":"string"},"issuer":{"description":"Only this issuer's cards.","enum":["amex","bank-of-america","barclays","caltech-efcu","capital-one","chase","citi","column","discover","elan","goldman-sachs","navy-federal","penfed","sofi","synchrony","td-bank","usbank","wells-fargo"],"type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"cash: cash back cards only. points: points and miles c